  "instructions": "## 3 V from a 9 V battery\n\nA sensor needs a **3.0 V** reference, and all you have is a 9 V battery and resistors. R1 is fixed at 1 kΩ; R2 is yours to choose.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Use the divider formula to find R2 so that the output at `n2` is 3.0 V.\n2. Set R2 with the slider (or type the exact value) and confirm with the voltmeter between `n2` and `GND`.\n3. Answer the question about the current the divider wastes.",
